.TH ZDOTS-INGEST-MEDIA 1 "2026-11-02" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-ingest-media \- ingest a media source into the knowledge pipeline
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-ingest-media --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: zdots-ingest-media <url|file> [options]
  --label <text>          Non-PHI display label (REQUIRED for local files)
  --profile <p>           Whisper profile (default: standard)
  --primer-text <text>    Source context for transcription and distillation
  --tags <list>           Comma-separated source tags for scoped known terms
  --num-speakers <n>      Diarization speaker-count hint (e.g. interviewees + 1)
  --force                 Reprocess an already-ingested source
  --journey-id <uuid>     Optional external work-item journey identity
  --run-id <uuid>         Optional Panoramic execution identity
  --correlation-id <uuid> Optional async message correlation identity
  --workflow-id <name>   Comparable workflow family name
  --flow-id <version>    Immutable contract identifier
  --run-class <class>    operational or control cohort
  --panoramic-started-at <iso8601> Run start for whole-path latency
  -h, --help              Show this help

Bot-gated sources (e.g. YouTube) need cookies. Set one of (opt-in):
  ZDOTS_YTDLP_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER=firefox   # interactive shell only (macOS TCC restricts launchd)
  ZDOTS_YTDLP_COOKIES_FILE=/path/to/cookies.txt # Netscape format; required for background worker
  (If cookie extraction fails, anonymous fetch is automatically attempted as fallback)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
